(a) the feedback received from key capitals including the US, UK, France, Germany, Israel and Japan following the visits by seven parliamentary delegations to 33 countries propagating India’s zero-terror tolerance post-Operation Sindoor;
(b) the areas of active cooperation endorsed such as security partnerships, counter-terrorism collaboration, or FATF coordination cited by foreign interlocutors; and
(c) the measures undertaken by the Ministry to collate, analyse and integrate this foreign feedback into India’s future counter-terror diplomacy and multilateral advocacy?

(a) whether the Ministry has conducted any veterinary infrastructure mapping in backward districts like Basti, Devipatan, and Saharanpur; 
(b) the number and status of mobile veterinary units, dispensaries, and Artificial Intelligence (AI) centres operational in these areas;
(c) whether rural women have been trained under livestock entrepreneurship or animal care modules; and
(d) the number of trainees placed or financially supported for self-employment since 2022?

SR

(a) the national progress of the PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana and PM KUSUM Scheme, including subsidies for women entrepreneurs and the solarization of agricultural assets; 
(b) the solarization of tubewells and involvement of FPOs in Uttar Pradesh, and the impact on local communities, including reduced energy costs, increased agricultural productivity and empowerment of women through leadership roles in FPOs managing solar assets; and
(c) the utilization of subsidies for women entrepreneurs to solarize tubewells in Etawah’s Barhpur block, the priority given to FPOs led by OBC women in managing solar assets and the reduction of diesel dependency?

(a) the national progress of the UP MSME Policy 2025, including interest subsidies for technology upgradation and the adoption of solar-powered looms;
(b) the implementation of the policy in the State of Uttar Pradesh, with details on support measures such as access to affordable credit, technology adoption incentives and observed benefits for handloom units, including increased productivity and market access; and
(c) the benefits to Etawah’s and Auraiya’s handloom units from interest subsidies for solar-powered looms and the facilitation of e-commerce partnerships through the One District One Product - Government e Marketplace (ODOP-GeM)?

(a) the national progress of the PM Awas Yojana-Urban’s (PMAY-U) Affordable Rental Housing Complexes (ARHCs), including gender-inclusive guidelines;
(b) the extension of ARHCs to peri-urban areas in the State of Uttar Pradesh, including efforts to address housing shortages for migrant workers, promote inclusive urban development and ensure access to basic amenities in newly developed residential areas; and
(c) the extension of ARHCs to Auraiya-Etawah’s peri-urban areas for seasonal migrant workers, with at least 25 per cent of units reserved for women-headed households?

(a) whether the Ministry has identified industrially backward districts such as Chitrakoot, Devipatan, and Jhansi for investment under Central schemes like the Production Linked Incentive (PLI) Scheme or cluster-based industrial parks; 
(b) the current status of projects, if any, approved in these areas under Samarth Udyog or Make in India initiatives; 
(c) whether any coordination has been undertaken with State Governments to provide infrastructure and skill support for heavy machinery, electronics, or defence-linked manufacturing in rural Uttar Pradesh; and 
(d) if not, whether the Ministry proposes to consider such districts for targeted industrial development in the next five-year investment cycle?

J

(a) the details of financial assistance provided to rural sports infrastructure in districts across the country since 2021 under Khelo India Scheme with a focus on popular sports like cricket and football;
(b) the rural sports initiatives launched in Uttar Pradesh to identify and support youth athletes, especially from OBC and marginalized backgrounds; and
(c) whether any rural sports infrastructure in Auraiya or Etawah has been sanctioned under Khelo India Scheme and whether a special initiative would be launched to support OBC youth athletes from aspirational blocks in these districts?

(a) the measures adopted under the Nutrient Based Subsidy (NBS) Scheme and Pradhan Mantri Krishi Samrudhi Yojana to promote indigenous fertilizer production, balanced nutrient management and the trends in fertilizer consumption and production from 2022 to 2025;
(b) whether Uttar Pradesh has benefited from One Nation One Fertilizer initiative and Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) for fertilizers, if so, the details thereof, including the number of farmers covered, total subsidy transferred and improvements in timely fertilizer availability; and
(c) the targeted fertilizer distribution and awareness campaigns conducted in Etawah and Auraiya and support provided to small and marginal farmers for soil health management and adoption of Nano-Urea or bio-fertilizers?

(a) whether Government’s Nai Roshni scheme has played a significant role in empowering minority women across the country through leadership training and social awareness programmes;
(b) the total number of women trained under this scheme nationwide since its inception and the share of beneficiaries belonging to the State of Uttar Pradesh;
(c) the number of districts in Uttar Pradesh currently covered under this Scheme and whether any plans to expand the programme to uncovered or aspirational districts; and
(d) the extent of convergence of Nai Roshni scheme with other schemes of women’s empowerment, digital literacy and livelihood generation in the State?

(a) the national disbursement of scholarships under Nai Udaan and Maulana Azad Fellowship schemes;
(b) the outreach efforts and number of beneficiaries in the State of  Uttar Pradesh under these schemes, including steps to increase awareness and application rates among minority students; and
(c) the measures taken to simplify application processes and raise awareness in rural areas of Auraiya?

(a) whether any Special Economic Zones, export promotion councils or MSME outreach clusters are being developed in Auraiya, Gorakhpur and Etawah districts;
(b) the level of participation of SHGs or rural entrepreneurs in export-related schemes like Market Access Initiative (MAI) and Trade Infrastructure for Export Scheme (TIES);
(c) whether these districts have benefitted from logistics park or e-commerce connectivity support; and
(d) the Ministry’s future action plan to integrate rural MSMEs into national and international supply chains?

(a) the measures taken to register farm women engaged in livestock, dairy, poultry and field crop operations under e-Shram across India, ensuring access to social protection and health insurance;
(b) the progress of e-Shram registration for women agricultural workers in Uttar Pradesh and the outreach strategies used to cover rural and semi-urban populations; and
(c) whether farm women in Auraiya district, where women constitute nearly 46.36 per cent of the population, are being formally registered as agricultural workers and the steps taken to ensure they fully avail the benefits of this initiative?

(a) the national progress of the Pradhan Mantri Janjatiya Vikas Mission (PMJVM), including the establishment of Van Dhan Vikas Kendras and market access for Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs);
(b) the inclusion of PVTGs in Uttar Pradesh and the strategies employed for their upliftment, such as livelihood support programs, skill development initiatives and efforts to enhance market access for tribal products and crafts; and
(c) the inclusion of PVTGs in Etawah’s Chambal ravines in the Janjatiya Vikas Mission and the establishment of Van Dhan Vikas Kendras or tribal haat bazaars in Etawah’s Chambal region?

(a) the number of AYURGYAN Scheme projects approved since Financial Year 2021–22, given the scheme’s aim to support research, innovation, capacity building, continuing medical education (CME) and information exchange in AYUSH systems;
(b) the total central funding allocated under AYURGYAN with specific details of funds earmarked for Uttar Pradesh;
(c) the number of CME events or training programmes conducted in UP particularly via Gorakhpur’s Mahayogi Guru Gorakhnath AYUSH University under AYURGYAN; and
(d) whether any research outputs or educational modules have been developed or piloted in UP and if so, the details of evaluation of these measures for impact on educational quality or practitioner competence?

(a) whether it is a fact that India’s largest crude-oil explorer, ONGC, in collaboration with BPCL, is planning to establish a 9 million tonne per annum refinery-cum-petrochemical complex at Prayagraj, Uttar Pradesh, at an estimated cost of over ?70,000 crore;
(b) if so, the current status of land acquisition, environmental clearances and project sanctioning;
(c) anticipated direct and indirect employment generation for Uttar Pradesh residents during construction and operations;
(d) projected annual fiscal benefits (such as State revenue, royalty, downstream industrial growth) accruing to Uttar Pradesh; and
(e) estimated timeline for commencement of construction and commissioning of the refinery?

(a) whether Government is aware that a substantial portion of India’s urban population resides in slum areas and if so, the details of initiatives taken under central schemes such as PMAY-Urban, AMRUT and SBM-U to improve housing and civic amenities for such communities; 
(b) the number of beneficiaries and the scale of implementation of these schemes in Uttar Pradesh; 
(c) whether Meerut district has been covered under these schemes and if so, the number of houses sanctioned, completed and occupied along with provision of water supply, sanitation and other basic infrastructure; and 
(d) the total central financial assistance allocated and utilised in Meerut under these schemes?

(a) whether the Ministry has identified tourism potential in underdeveloped yet heritage-rich districts such as Ayodhya, Etawah and Bundelkhand for development under Swadesh Darshan or PRASHAD schemes;
(b) the number and status of rural infrastructure projects sanctioned in these locations for tourism enhancement;
(c) whether Government has created homestay models, cultural circuits or livelihood generation plans linked to tourism; and
(d) the quantum of rural employment generated and role of local women in such projects?

(a) the national progress of the Eklavya Model Residential Schools (EMRSs) scheme, including the extension to tribal-dominated areas;
(b) the inclusion of tribal villages in Uttar Pradesh, with details on implementation challenges and successes, efforts to improve access to quality education and initiatives to address dropout rates and promote cultural preservation among tribal communities; and
(c) the extension of EMRS to Auraiya-Etawah’s tribal-dominated villages and the priority access to national scholarships and reserved seats for EMRS students?

(a) the national compliance status of fortified foodgrain distribution under National Food Security Act (NFSA), covering 75 per cent rural and 50 per cent urban populations; 
(b) the utilization of ?40,093 crore allocated to Uttar Pradesh under Pradhan Mantri Garib Kalyan Anna Yojana (PMGKAY) for 14.71 crore beneficiaries; and
(c) the plans to expand smart ration card systems or Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) in Auraiya’s 16 lakh NFSA beneficiaries to reduce leakages, as flagged in Jal Jeevan Mission audits?

(a) the district-wise status of household electrification in tribal-dominated areas in the State of Uttar Pradesh, including the number of villages still lacking electricity connection;
(b) the total funds allocated and utilized during the last five years for electrification projects in tribal regions in the State of Uttar Pradesh under Central schemes; and
(c) the measures taken by Government to ensure reliable power supply and infrastructure expansion in these tribal areas?

(a) the steps being taken to strengthen training infrastructure and academic programmes at the  Indira Gandhi Rashtriya Uran Akademi (IGRUA) and the National Aviation University (NAU);
(b) the measures adopted to align training courses with emerging skill requirements in the aviation sector, including pilot training, aircraft maintenance and aviation management; and
(c) whether any monitoring or evaluation mechanism has been laid down to assess training capacity, placement outcomes and contribution of these institutions to the aviation workforce in the country?

(a) the institutional arrangements and data governance standards adopted to ensure accuracy, consistency and timeliness of higher education statistics generated under Higher Education Statistics and Public Information System (HESPIS);
(b) the manner in which coordination is being ensured with universities, colleges and State authorities for regular data submission and validation; and
(c) whether any mechanism has been laid down to ensure effective use of HESPIS data for policy planning, performance review and addressing regional disparities in the higher education sector?

(a) the details of the latest Nutrient Based Subsidy (NBS) rates approved for phosphatic and potassic fertilizers for the current agricultural season and the estimated subsidy outlay thereof;
(b) whether Government has assessed the availability, distribution and sale of P&K fertilisers in States such as Uttar Pradesh under the revised NBS rates and the steps taken to ensure uninterrupted supply to farmers; and
(c) whether the Ministry is examining any further reforms to the NBS framework to improve subsidy efficiency and nutrient accessibility and if so, the broad contours of such reforms?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the impact of increasing the threshold for layoffs without prior Government approval from 100 to 300 workers;
(b) whether concerns regarding the definition of wages, inclusion criteria and coverage of workers in small establishments under the new Labour Codes have been examined;
(c) the details of steps taken to ensure that gig and platform workers are effectively included, under the Code on Social Security; and
(d) whether monitoring mechanisms or review processes have been instituted to evaluate the implementation of labour protections and social security measures for all categories of workers?

(a) whether the Centrally Sponsored Scheme for Development of Judicial Infrastructure has contributed to the expansion of court facilities, modernization and digital enablement of courts across the country;
(b) if so, the details of funds allocated, released and actually utilised in Uttar Pradesh under this scheme during the last three years, district-wise particularly for Auraiya; and
(c) the steps taken to further strengthen judicial infrastructure, enhance digital facilities and improve access to justice in the State, particularly in districts like Auraiya?

(a) the criteria adopted for selection of Industrial Training Institutes (ITIs) proposed to be modernised under the PM-SETU initiative and the nature of upgradation planned;
(b) the arrangements made to strengthen industry participation in curriculum design, training delivery and apprenticeship opportunities to improve job readiness of trainees; and
(c) whether any monitoring or evaluation mechanism has been put in place to assess improvements in placement outcomes, employability skills and industry acceptance of trainees trained under the initiative?

(a) the approach being followed to strengthen functional capacities of Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRIs) through training and handholding under Rashtriya Gram Swaraj Abhiyan (RGSA);
(b) the steps taken to integrate e-Panchayat platforms with planning, budgeting and service delivery functions at the Gram Panchayat level; and
(c) whether any monitoring or evaluation framework has been laid down to assess progress in localisation of Sustainable Development Goals through Panchayat-led planning under the Abhiyan?

(a) the guidelines being followed for extending the waiver of inter state transmission system (ISTS) charges to renewable energy projects;
(b) the arrangements made to ensure timely grid connectivity and evacuation for projects availing the waiver; and
(c) whether any review mechanism has been put in place to assess the effect of the waiver on project viability and grid utilisation?

(a) whether internal monitoring systems capture DISCOM-wise actual versus scheduled load delivery, seasonal load shedding events, and granular AT&C loss breakdowns at feeder or ward levels, beyond State-level performance figures;
(b) if so, the comparative internal performance summaries for the State of Uttar Pradesh, including rural distribution segments; and
(c) whether Auraiya district-specific load reliability records, feeder-wise loss indices, and consumer complaint resolution timelines are maintained in internal dashboards that are not publicly available, and the measures taken to utilise such data for improving electricity distribution efficiency?

(a) whether the Production Linked Incentive (PLI) Scheme for automobile and auto components has attracted investment and enhanced manufacturing capacity at the national level;
(b) if so, the number of approved applicants, investment commitments and production outcomes reported for Uttar Pradesh; and
(c) whether district-wise data for Auraiya indicates any ancillary manufacturing activity, employment generation or participation in the supply chain linked to the scheme?

(a) the key achievements under the Remission of Duties and Taxes on Exported Products (RoDTEP) scheme since its implementation;
(b) the total amount of remission disbursed under RoDTEP during 2021–22 to 2025–26, sector-wise and year-wise;
(c) the number of exporters benefited under RoDTEP during 2021–22 to 2025–26;
(d) the major product categories notified with applicable rates to enhance the competitiveness of Indian exports; and
(e) the steps taken to improve transparency and efficiency through digital implementation of the scheme and the proposals, if any, for expansion of product coverage or revision of notified rates?

(a) the total allocation made for restructuring of the Krishonnati Yojana in the Union Budget 2026, along with the main components and purposes for which funds are earmarked;
(b) the specific targets or benchmarks set under the Yojana for enhancing farmers’ income, including timelines and measurable indicators;
(c) the mechanisms proposed for tracking and measuring income improvements at the farmer level under Krishonnati Yojana, including data sources and reporting systems; and
(d) the manner in which the Krishonnati Yojana is planned to integrate with other Central and State schemes related to irrigation, crop diversification, market access and price support to achieve holistic impact?

(a) the key objectives and components of the Bharat-VISTAAR platform;
(b) the total allocation made for the Bharat-VISTAAR platform in the Union Budget 2026, along with the main components and purposes for which funds are earmarked;
(c) the planned timeline for phased rollout of the platform and the indicative coverage in terms of districts, languages and categories of farmers targeted in the initial phase;
(d) whether the design framework of Bharat-VISTAAR incorporates safeguards relating to data privacy, transparency of Artificial intelligence (AI) systems and equitable access for small and marginal farmers; and
(e) if so, the details of the broad features of such safeguards?

(a) the implementation status of Prime Minister’s Development Initiative for North East (PM-DevINE) scheme, State-wise;
(b) the infrastructure projects completed in connectivity, power, water and social sectors, State-wise;
(c) whether the Ministry has assessed the extent to which development gaps have been addressed under the scheme;
(d) if so, the details thereof, State-wise;
(e) whether Government proposes to extend the scheme beyond its current period; and
(f) if so, the details thereof, State-wise?

(a) the current status of projects supported under the National Culture Fund (NCF) during the last three years, including funds collected and projects completed, State-wise;
(b) the details of measures taken to strengthen public-private partnership framework under the Fund and to increase the participation of private sector and public institutions;
(c) the details of contributions made by NCF-supported initiatives in preservation, promotion, and dissemination of cultural heritage across the country; and
(d) whether the Ministry has conducted any review or impact assessment of effectiveness, transparency and outcomes of NCF and if so, the findings thereof?

(a) the major initiatives undertaken by the Department of Posts to strengthen its presence in parcel and e-commerce logistics, including technological upgrades, logistics modernisation and tie-ups with domestic and global e-commerce platforms;
(b) the growth recorded in parcel traffic and logistics services during the last three years and measures adopted to enhance market competitiveness and service reliability;
(c) whether the Department has assessed the impact of these initiatives on revenue generation and operational efficiency; and
(d) if so, the details thereof, including financial performance indicators and future expansion strategy?

(a) the financial performance of India Post Payments Bank (IPPB) during the last three years, including customer accounts, amounts of transactions and services offered across the country;
(b) the role of IPPB in women empowerment, rural customers and employment generation particularly in North-Eastern Regions (NER) and backward/aspirational districts of Uttar Pradesh;
(c) whether IPPB has achieved financial viability; and
(d) if so, the assessment details thereof?

(a) the progress under scheme of opening Post Office Passport Seva Kendras (POPSKs) in all Lok Sabha Constituencies, including those operational, circle-wise;
(b) the number of applications processed during the last three years and the details of new services started;
(c) whether the Ministry has assessed the impact of the initiative on passport access; and
(d) if so, the findings thereof?

(a) whether the PM SHRI Schools scheme has been implemented across States to upgrade selected Government schools in accordance with prescribed infrastructure, digital learning and green school norms;
(b) if so, the number of schools selected and currently functional under the scheme in Uttar Pradesh, along with details of the key intervention components approved for these schools; and
(c) whether district-wise details for Auraiya indicates progress in infrastructure upgradation, teacher capacity-building and student enrolment trends in the PM SHRI Schools identified under the scheme if so, the measures taken to address any gaps or delays?

(a) whether the Ministry has decided to introduce mandatory sunset clauses for all Central Government schemes from 2026 onwards, as part of efforts to improve fiscal discipline, administrative efficiency and performance evaluation;
(b) whether the likely administrative and operational impact of introducing such clauses has been assessed, if so, the details thereof; 
(c) the measures proposed/ taken to ensure that the introduction of sunset clauses does not disrupt ongoing schemes or affect beneficiaries adversely; and
(d) whether Government plans to monitor and evaluate the performance of schemes under these clauses to ensure timely decision-making regarding continuation, modification, or closure of schemes?

(a) whether Government has issued any clear and enforceable guidelines that define the scope of practice, referral procedures and clinical responsibilities of Ayush practitioners working in integrated or co-located healthcare facilities;
(b) the details of the implementation of guidelines across all States and Union Territories; and
(c) the steps being taken by Government to ensure consistent compliance with these guidelines to improve coordination between Ayush and modern medical systems and safeguard patient care standards?

(a) whether Government has identified mineral-bearing sites suitable for auction in districts of western Uttar Pradesh such as Etawah, Auraiya, Firozabad, Mainpuri and Etah;
(b) if so, the details of mineral blocks notified, auctioned or proposed for auction in this region, along with the current status of allocation and exploration;
(c) whether any the Central or State reports have been prepared regarding the potential value and commercial viability of these mineral resources; and
(d) the extent to which the planned or ongoing auctions in western Uttar Pradesh are expected to contribute to local employment opportunities, revenue enhancement and overall industrial development within the State?

(a) current status of the regional connectivity scheme (UDAN), including the number of routes operational, number of underserved airports connected and capacity utilisation during the last three years;
(b) details of passenger traffic growth and aircraft movement data at tier-II and tier-III airports, including performance indicators such as on-time departures and cancellations;
(c) specific operational challenges identified such as crew shortages, ground handling constraints and weather-related disruptions; and
(d) measures taken to improve airport infrastructure, air traffic management and regional airline viability, and whether any review has been undertaken to recalibrate subsidies, airport charges or slot allocations to boost regional connectivity sustainability?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the recent decline in merchandise export growth during 2025;
(b) the sectors that have been most affected by the global slowdown in demand;
(c) whether any expansion of support measures under the Foreign Trade Policy, 2023, is under consideration, particularly to assist exporters in Uttar Pradesh;
(d) whether special credit lines for Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSME) exporters, including those operating from emerging export clusters in Uttar Pradesh, are being explored; and
(e) the steps being taken to stabilise and strengthen India’s export performance in 2026?

(a) whether Government is aware that the proposed highway near Kaziranga National Park, a UNESCO world heritage site, involves diversion of nearly 20 hectares of forest land from the core area and around 364 hectares from its Eco-Sensitive Zone;
(b) the likely impact of such diversion on wildlife movement between Kaziranga and the Karbi Anglong hills and on the park’s ecological balance;
(c) whether the National Board for Wildlife, while granting clearance in February 2024, prescribed safeguards; and
(d) the steps taken or proposed by Government, including monitoring and enforcement mechanisms?

(a) whether Government has examined gaps in digital infrastructure, including poor internet connectivity and lack of access to digital devices in rural, tribal, and economically weaker areas, affecting digital learning under NEP, 2020;
(b) the extent of these gaps in schools and among students at home, particularly in underserved regions;
(c) whether any specific measures or dedicated funds have been provided to bridge these digital infrastructure gaps in the four years since NEP, 2020 was launched; and
(d) the initiatives planned or undertaken to improve connectivity, provide digital devices and enhance access to online learning resources for students in rural, tribal and economically weaker areas?

(a) whether national data under AB-PMJAY shows an increase in hospital admissions and claim settlements following the expansion of beneficiary coverage, as reflected in the official dashboards;
(b) if so, the corresponding figures for Uttar Pradesh over the last three financial years, including the total number of beneficiaries treated and claims settled; and
(c) whether data for Auraiya district is available, showing trends in the utilization of secondary and tertiary care services, the number of empanelled hospitals and the average claim value under the scheme?

(a) the number of tuberculosis (TB) patients registered under the National TB Elimination Programme (NTEP), along with details of the number of patients who have received the monthly nutritional assistance in the last three years, State-wise;
(b) whether, despite an increase in nutritional support, a number of TB patients have faced delays or non-receipt of payments, and if so, the reasons therefor; and
(c) the steps being taken by Government to ensure timely Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) to all eligible TB patients under the scheme, and the timeline for clearing all pending payments?

(a) details of the total funds released and utilised under the MPLADS across all constituencies in the State of Uttar Pradesh during the last five financial years, including year-wise trends and constituency-wise utilisation rates;
(b) whether any cases of delayed implementation, unspent allocations or diversion of funds have been reported during this period and the action taken thereon; and
(c) whether Government has undertaken performance or social audits to assess the effectiveness and timeliness of MPLADS works, particularly in rural and tribal constituencies and if so, the key findings and steps taken to strengthen transparency, monitoring and accountability mechanisms under the scheme?

(a) the number of micro food-processing units established so far under the Pradhan Mantri Formalisation of Micro Food Processing Enterprises (PMFME) scheme;
(b)whether the Ministry has assessed the pace of implementation in view of substantial funds released;
(c) whether the Ministry has identified districts in Uttar Pradesh where uptake of PMFME support remains low despite strong agricultural production; and
(d) whether any targeted interventions are being planned to support micro-entrepreneurs in such districts and to enhance local food-processing value addition?

(a) national progress of the Purvodaya initiative for green hydrogen production and energy transition, including the establishment of training centres and skill development hubs;
(b) integration of training programs with ITIs in Uttar Pradesh and the outcomes achieved, including increased enrolment in technical courses, enhanced employability of local youth and collaboration with industry partners to provide hands-on training and job placement support; and
(c) establishment of training centres and skill development hubs in or near Auraiya-Etawah, the integration of these programs with ITI Auraiya under Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) 4.0 and provision of employment opportunities for local OBC youth?

(a) whether Ghazipur and Varanasi river ports have been selected under Sagarmala Phase III for modernization and mechanisation;
(b) whether dredging, berthing facility enhancement and development of warehousing terminals are being expedited;
(c) whether any financial or technical partnership with private players, under PPP modalities, has been initiated; and
(d) whether the Ministry has set a timeline for full operationalisation, including handling of exports of agricultural produce from Uttar Pradesh by the end of the year 2026?

(a) the national progress of the UP MSME Policy 2025, including interest subsidies for technology upgradation and the adoption of solar-powered looms;
(b) the implementation of the policy in the State of Uttar Pradesh, with details on support measures such as access to affordable credit, technology adoption incentives and observed benefits for handloom units, including increased productivity and market access; and
(c) the benefits to Etawah’s and Auraiya’s handloom units from interest subsidies for solar-powered looms and the facilitation of e-commerce partnerships through the One District One Product - Government e Marketplace (ODOP-GeM)?

(a) whether the Ministry has undertaken a review of regional language content availability on Doordarshan and All India Radio, including new programme additions in the past two years;
(b) whether regional broadcasting centres have reported constraints relating to staffing, production equipment or digital-broadcasting infrastructure and the findings of such assessments; and
(c) whether the Ministry proposes expanding community level media literacy, content-creation hubs or regional production facilities for underserved linguistic groups?

(a) the extent to which beneficiaries under the Production Linked Incentive (PLI) Scheme for automobile and auto components have met localisation and value-addition commitments, including components with persistent import dependence;
(b) whether any independent or third-party audits have been conducted to verify investment claims, production-linked achievements and localisation data submitted by beneficiaries; and
(c) whether the Ministry proposes dedicated support for MSMEs within the auto-component supply chain to upgrade machinery, enhance testing capability and achieve PLI-aligned standards?

(a) the progress of implementation of e-Courts Phase-III project, including digital records, virtual hearings and case management systems, as highlighted in the Supreme Court e-Committee’s recent review;
(b) whether the Ministry has discussed vacancy levels, infrastructure gaps and digital enablement challenges with the Uttar Pradesh judiciary, especially in high-pendency districts and the nature of outcomes from such consultations; and
(c) whether the Ministry proposes new e-Court facilities, training programmes or infrastructure upgrades for courts in Auraiya district?

(a) the status of CPGRAMS grievance disposal, including pendency trends and Ministry-wise performance indicators as reported in the latest DARPG dashboard;
(b) whether Government has consulted the State Government of Uttar Pradesh regarding district-level grievance trends, frequent categories of complaints and administrative bottlenecks in timely disposal and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether steps are proposed to strengthen grievance-handling capacity in Auraiya, including training of nodal officers and integration with State-level digital grievance systems and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Ministry has reviewed the implementation of foundational literacy and numeracy interventions under Samagra Shiksha at the national level and if so, the findings regarding student learning outcomes;
(b) whether Uttar Pradesh’s performance on key indicators such as teacher availability, digital infrastructure and school preparedness has been analysed; and
(c) whether districts demonstrating learning gaps, including Auraiya wherever relevant, are being considered for strengthened academic-support interventions or targeted monitoring?

(a) whether the Ministry has reviewed compliance and governance performance under the amended Multi-State Cooperative Societies (MSCS) framework at the national level and if so, the findings regarding societies requiring enhanced oversight;
(b) whether the Ministry has examined the functioning of MSCS operating in the State of Uttar Pradesh, especially in sectors such as dairy, credit and housing, in relation to the new audit and transparency norms; 
(c) whether district-level cooperative institutions have been considered for support in streamlining compliance workflows through dedicated facilitation desks and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has recently assessed persistent issues in CSR implementation, including regional concentration of funds, uneven sectoral allocation and concerns that CSR impact remains limited despite rising expenditure;
(b) whether the Ministry has analysed CSR-MIS data to identify States such as Uttar Pradesh which continue to receive comparatively lower CSR inflows and the reasons for sustained under-allocation to less industrialised districts; and
(c) whether, in view of recent penalty actions against companies for non-transfer or misuse of CSR funds, the Ministry proposes to strengthen compliance monitoring and introduce enhanced transparency requirements for firms repeatedly found non-compliant?

(a) the present status of modernisation initiatives of the Targeted Public Distribution System (TPDS), including portability under the One Nation One Ration Card (ONORC) framework, ePoS-based authentication and digitisation of ration cards;
(b) the district-wise progress of Fortified Rice distribution in Uttar Pradesh under TPDS and the steps taken by the Ministry to address any supply-chain or operational challenges in the State; and
(c) whether Government proposes to extend additional support for improving digital payment facilities, electronic weighing systems and grievance-redress mechanisms at Fair Price Shops, particularly in rural districts such as Auraiya?

(a) whether Government has reviewed compliance with minor mineral extraction rules in the State of Uttar Pradesh following recent reports of illegal sand mining in Sonebhadra and Ghaziabad districts, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the amount collected under the District Mineral Foundation (DMF) in the State and utilisation status till December, 2025 for the last three financial years;
(c) whether the funds have been allocated to priority areas like water conservation, school education and tribal welfare in affected districts; and
(d) the steps taken to strengthen real-time monitoring and satellite tracking of mining activities in the State?

(a) progress made in implementing green aviation initiatives, including Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF) blending targets, carbon-neutral airport infrastructure and emission reduction programmes, along with data on investments, emission cuts and efficiency gains as of December, 2025;
(b) whether the State of Uttar Pradesh has undertaken any sustainable airport or SAF initiatives and if so, the details thereof, including airports involved, investment scale, partnerships and environmental outcomes; and
